    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310539": {
      "title": "Campus Safety and Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety and Security Officer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Safety and Security Officer Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $17.00 - $19.00 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level High School Apply Description Campus Security Officer The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Campus Security Officer position. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Campus Security Supervisor/and Director of Campus Security. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Campus Security Officer. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : Full time Benefits Eligible Job Purpose: To provide and assist in the immediate protection and security of students, faculty, staff and visitors in various campus buildings and/or property within the university community by enforcing the policies and procedures set by the university, state, and local laws. Specific Job Duties: Respond to all calls for service in a timely and professional manner. Conduct investigations as required and document findings in accordance with department policies and procedures. Provide security and protective services to the campus community through routine patrols of assigned buildings, parking areas, and grounds. Respond to emergency situations by assessing conditions, exercising sound judgment, and using tact and diplomacy to maintain safety and restore order. Complete incident reports and other required documentation accurately and promptly. Maintain continuous radio communication with the dispatcher and other department personnel. Provide crowd management and traffic control during campus events, special activities, and emergency situations. Provide authorized access to campus buildings and verify the identity and authorization of individuals requesting entry. Identify safety hazards during patrols and promptly submit work orders or notify the appropriate university personnel for corrective action. Patrol campus parking areas to ensure compliance with parking regulations and issue citations when appropriate. Monitor fire lanes to ensure they remain unobstructed and take appropriate enforcement action in accordance with university policy. Provide safety escorts to students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a timely and professional manner. Maintain a thorough knowledge of campus facilities, roadways, parking areas, and university operations to effectively respond to calls for service. Assist with the training and mentoring of newly assigned officers as directed by the training supervisor. Provide relief staffing for the Control Center as assigned. Secure campus buildings during assigned shifts by conducting routine security inspections of doors, windows, mechanical systems, and other critical building components. Contact Facilities Management or other appropriate personnel to coordinate emergency repairs or address maintenance-related concerns. Attend and successfully complete all required professional development, certifications, and in-service training. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Starting Salary: $17.00-$19.00 an hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: Shift will include evenings or overnights to meet needs of the department. Experience/Skills: Ability to communicate effectively and have the ability to understand, comprehend and follow directions Must have good teamwork skills Entry Level (Prior Law Enforcement, security, or military experience preferred). Physical Demands: Prolonged standing/setting/wrist movement Prolonged walking significant distances between and within building on campus often in adverse weather conditions. Ability to lift 50lbs. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to read, interpret, and follow printed materials, instructions, and procedures. Ability to remain calm under pressure, respond appropriately in emergency situations, and communicate effectively with the appropriate authorities. Strong attention to detail and the ability to accurately recall events for incident and report documentation. Proficiency with basic computer applications and general computer skills. Preferred qualifications: CPR Certified AED Certified Education: High school diploma or equivalent education Certified by the State of Virginia Department of Criminal Justice Services as a CSO within 180 days of employment Valid Virginia State Vehicle Operator's License Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310527": {
      "title": "Website Manager & Content Strategist",
      "description": "Website Manager & Content Strategist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Website Manager & Content Strategist Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $62,000.00 - $68,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Website Manager & Content Strategist The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Website Manager position in the Department of Marketing and Communications. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Executive Director of Marketing. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Website Manager and Content Strategist. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : FT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The Website Manager & Content Strategist is the technical and editorial owner of the University of Lynchburg's digital presence. This is a strategic role responsible for the intersection of content strategy, web performance, and AI-driven discoverability. The Website Manager ensures our digital platforms serve prospective students, current students, faculty, and the broader community with clarity and speed, while serving as the bridge between creative marketing goals and technical execution. Specific Job Duties: Develop and own the University's web content strategy, including voice, structure, and editorial standards across all digital platforms. Build and enforce a centralized content intake and governance model to manage requests from departments across the University. Execute hands-on website updates and page builds using WordPress and Elementor, reorganizing content for web best practices and audience clarity. Audit, map, and continuously improve site navigation and information architecture to reduce friction for prospective students and other key audiences. Manage the WP Engine hosting environment, including staging and production workflows, server-side performance optimization, and plugin governance. Establish and maintain global Elementor templates and design guidelines to ensure a cohesive brand presence across all web platforms. Ensure 100% of site content meets WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards and own the annual audit and remediation process. Optimize content for both traditional organic search and AI-discovery engines, including structured data, FAQ strategy, and entity-based content approaches. Own GA4 implementation and deliver monthly analytics reports to leadership connecting web performance to enrollment funnel metrics. Identify and implement AI-assisted tools to accelerate content production, metadata generation, and A/B testing while maintaining brand and accuracy standards Maintain and develop an editorial calendar aligned to the academic year, admissions cycle, and University events. Supervise the student Digital Media Assistant and serve as a mentor for emerging web and content professionals. Collaborate across departments via Asana, email, and Google Workspace while enforcing centralized governance standards. Starting Salary: $62,000-$68,000 Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required) Qualifications Experience/Skills: Minimum of 5 year of progressive experience in website management, digital content strategy, or web marketing, preferably in higher education or a mission-driven organization. Demonstrated experience owning a large, multi-stakeholder website (500+pages) from both a strategic and technical standpoint. Proven track record of developing and executing a content strategy that improved measurable outcomes such as traffic, leads, time-on-site, or enrollment inquires. Background working in environments with decentralized content contributors and centralized governance, ideally in higher education, healthcare, or government. Advanced, hands-on experience with WordPress and Elementor, including custom CSS, template hierarchy, and plugin management. Proficiency with WP Engine's hosting platform, staging environments, CDN configuration, and performance tooling. Working expertise in technical SEO, including Core Web Vitals, schema markup, canonical tags, and XML sitemaps. Solid working knowledge of HTML and CSS sufficient to write and debug custom code within WordPress. Experience auditing and remediating WCAG 2.1 AA issues using tools such as Siteimprove, axe, or WAVE. Familiarity with AI writing assistants and emerging LLM-powered content tools such as Gemini, Notebook LM, ChatGPT, Claude, Jasper, or Surfer SEO. Experience with project management and intake tools such as Asana, Monday.com, or similar platforms. Strong written communication skills and ability to enforce editorial standards across a large organization. Physical Demands: Prolonged sitting and wrist movement Required Qualifications: Minimum of 5 years of experience in website management or digital content strategy. Advanced proficiency in WordPress and Elementor. Demonstrated knowledge of SEO best practices and GA4 analytics. Working knowledge of WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards. Preferred qualifications: Experience in a higher education marketing or communications environment, with fluency in the enrollment funnel as it applies to prospective students. Familiarity with CRM integrations such as Slate or Salesforce and how web forms connect to enrollment systems. Experience with heatmap and UX research tools such as Hotjar or Microsoft Clarity. Working knowledge of email marketing platforms and how web content connects to audience nurture campaigns. Experience with AI-powered SEO tools such as Surfer, Clearscope, or SEMrush AI, and an understanding of how large language models surface institutional content. Background in brand management or experience maintaining a design system or style guide at scale. Certifications in Google Analytics, HubSpot Content, or a recognized SEO platform. Experience with video, podcast, or multimedia content strategy as the University expands its content formats. Education: Bachelor's Degree in Communication, Marketing, Journalism, Information Science, or a related field. Equivalent experience may be considered. Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/06E60EB4A3425A1B8B2E3A5F3F1E2A6F/jobs/310266": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Counselor Lynchburg  - Lynchburg, VA 24501 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.77 Hourly Position Type Staff Job Shift Full time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Admissions Counselor The University of Lynchburg , a private, regional university in the beautiful foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Central Virginia, is seeking applicants for full-time, Admissions Counselor position in Undergraduate Admissions. This position reports to, is supervised by, and evaluated by the Director of Admissions. The evaluation of work performance will be ongoing and will be carried out by the Admissions Counselor. It will include the specific duties and responsibilities of this position description plus employee attitude and general working behavior. Job Type : FT (Benefits Eligible) Job Purpose: The primary focus of the Admissions Counselor is to build strong, lasting relationships with prospective students, guiding and supporting them through every stage of the college choice process—including program selection, application completion, admission evaluation, financial aid navigation, and final enrollment. Representing the institution to prospective students, families, high school guidance counselors, and community organizations, this position executes data-informed territory recruitment plans to contribute directly to institutional enrollment goals. Specific Job Duties: Territory Management & Strategy: Plan, manage, and execute targeted recruitment strategies within an assigned geographic territory to meet individual inquiry, applicant, and enrollment goals. Develop and maintain territory data to inform strategic travel itineraries and outreach plans. Multi-Channel Student Outreach: Utilize phone, email, text messaging, and social media outreach proactively to cultivate personalized relationships with prospective students and families, guiding them from inquiry to matriculation. Application Review & Admissions Decisions: Review candidate application files thoroughly, evaluate transcripts and credentials, and render admissions decisions in compliance with institutional standards. CRM Workflow & Data Tracking (Slate): Manage prospective student records in Slate CRM. Record all conversations, campus touchpoints, and recruitment interactions to drive personalized communication workflows and yield tracking. Campus Visits, Presentations & On-Campus Interviews: Conduct individual student/family interviews, deliver engaging group presentations, and lead information sessions for visiting students, families, and college counseling personnel. Event Participation & Field Recruitment: Represent the institution at on-campus and off-campus recruitment events, college fairs, high school visits, and community outreach programs. Counselor & Community Relationship Building: Develop long-standing relationships with high school counselors and community-based organizations (CBOs), designing collaborative opportunities to bring students and advisors to campus. Special Project Ownership & Operational Support: Manage or oversee a specialized operational project (e.g., Student Ambassador leadership, campus tour program management, digital outreach initiatives, or transfer credit liaison work) to support enrollment goals. Committee Governance & Professional Development: Serve on campus committees related to student development (orientation, leadership, retention). Participate in national/regional professional organizations (e.g., NACAC, SACAC/VACAC) for continuous development. Basic Financial Aid & Affordability Counseling: Guiding prospective students and families through FAFSA completion steps, merit scholarship qualifications, and cost of attendance estimates. Targeted Yield & Conversion Campaign Execution: Executing phone marathons, admitted student outreach campaigns, and personalized decision follow-ups during peak yield season. Transfer & Diversity Pipeline Support: Partnering with community colleges and access organizations to expand non-traditional and underrepresented student recruitment. Other duties as assigned Starting Salary: $20.77 per hour Benefits: Generous paid vacation, personal days, paid sick time and family leave, comprehensive insurance (medical, dental, vision, etc.) and retirement plans, flexible spending account, tuition remission, life and long-term disability insurance, and more. Learn more about employment benefits at the University of Lynchburg. Schedule: 8:30 am - 5:00 pm (7.5 hours/day with some evenings and weekends to meet needs of the department may be required Qualifications Experience/Skills: Ability to communicate effectively and have the ability to understand, comprehend and follow directions Must have good teamwork skills Ability to write effectively Exceptional attention to details Strong proofreading skills Comfortable delivering presentations to small and large groups Physical Demands: Prolonged standing/sitting/wrist movement Long periods sitting in front of a computer screen Time spent traveling in motor vehicles/flights to and from recruitment events Limited lifting and carrying of luggage and recruitment collateral Ability to lift 20 lbs. Required Qualifications: 1-2 years of professional experience in sales, marketing recruitment, higher education, coaching, or another goal-oriented field Valid Drivers License Extensive travel required Education: Bachelor's Degree Work Remotely: No We seek candidates who are committed to the University of Lynchburg’s efforts to create an environment that fosters a student-centered environment, develops the breadth of knowledge associated with liberal education, respects and supports diversity, equity, and inclusion, values and celebrates diverse faith traditions, and sustains close working relationships among faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community partners. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Submit a cover letter, résumé, and three professional references to: Human Resources Jobs Page The University of Lynchburg is dedicated to inclusive excellence. We celebrate the diversity of our common life, affirming our different histories, realities, and identities. All belong here. As a testament to our strong commitment to accessibility, diversity, and inclusion, we will attract, celebrate, and retain a community of diverse students, staff, and faculty; foster belonging; and create a campus environment that embraces civil discourse and accountability for our words and actions. The University of Lynchburg embraces diversity in its broadest sense. We will cultivate an inclusive, equitable, and safe campus climate grounded in mutual respect and understanding, where all members of our diverse learning community - alumni, employees, learners, visitors, and volunteers- can thrive. The University of Lynchburg is an equal-opportunity employer. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
